// The same rise against fall split a strength reading uses, taken as a plain
// ratio of summed moves, so it swings the whole of its range rather than
// compressing towards the middle.
//
// Exercises a warmup one bar later than the plain reading would give: the first
// change is absent, so the first complete window of changes ends at bar `len`
// rather than at bar `len - 1`.

version 1

study("Chande momentum", overlay = false, precision = 4)

len = input(9, "Length", min = 1, max = 500)
src = input(close, "Source")

move = change(src)
rise = move >= 0 ? move : 0
fall = move >= 0 ? 0 : -move

// Both totals are taken once, at the top level. Only the taken arm of a ternary
// is evaluated, so a windowed total written inside one would advance only on the
// bars that arm was taken on.
rose  = sum(rise, len)
fell  = sum(fall, len)
total = rose + fell

// A perfectly flat window has nothing to divide by, and every finite answer
// invented there would be a reading of a market that did not move.
plot(total == 0 ? none : 100 * (rose - fell) / total, "Chande momentum", blue, width = 2)

level(0, "Zero", gray, style = "dashed")
